<p>The grid above shows a 16×16 block (256 tokens). At step 0, everything is [MASK] (grey). As you drag the slider forward, the model progressively commits tokens — green cells show locked tokens, amber shows high-confidence-but-not-yet-committed positions, grey shows tokens still being re-masked. By step 15–20, most common-context tokens are green; only the genuinely ambiguous ones keep iterating until step 48 or early stopping.</p>

<h3>15–20 tokens per forward pass</h3>
<p>Because only a fraction of the 256 canvas positions are committed per step, each forward pass effectively contributes 15–20 new tokens to the final output. Compared to AR's 1 token per pass, this is the source of the 15–20× reduction in forward passes — even if each pass is somewhat more expensive (bidirectional attention over 256 tokens).</p>
</section>

