<h3>The batch size cliff</h3>
<p>DiffusionGemma's throughput advantage is strongest at <strong>low batch sizes (batch=1 or small)</strong> — the typical scenario for local or single-user inference. At large batch sizes (typical for cloud API serving), autoregressive models use batching to keep their GPUs busy, and the advantage narrows. Google explicitly notes that standard Gemma 4 remains preferred for cloud deployments.</p>

